# Stations, sections and spans of the drivetrain (bom.ttl, placements.ttl) for the stations tests, in the shape the
# stations, spans and occurrence-spans CONSTRUCTs produce. Axis y, symmetric: ST 0 inferred, ST 300 joint, ST 600
# measured (tolerance 5 mm); S-C (FR, both, ST 0 to ST 300, the section the FR-only hinge is), S-R (DE, right) and S-L
# (UK, left), both ST 300 to ST 600. Spans in mm, the UK motor's in inches:
#   de-gear 400 to 450 (each of its three rows too); de-housing 280 to 320, no rows; fr-panel 50 to 150, its fr-kit rows
#   50 to 150 and 550 to 650, its cover-set rows 50 to 150; fr-hinge (FR only) 290 to 310; uk-motor 11.8110 to 15.7480
#   in, its rows the same and, turned 180 degrees about z, -15.7480 to -11.8110 in; es-frame -350 to 350; es-bracket 0 to
#   20, its rows 0 to 20 and, turned 90 degrees about x, -100 to 0.
# A three-level DE tree under de-kit: de-arm-set twice, the second 1000 mm along y and turned 180 degrees about z, >
# de-arm-pair twice, 50 mm apart along y, > de-arm (400 to 420, no rows): its true envelopes are 400 to 420, 450 to 470,
# 580 to 600 and 530 to 550.
